+Source: `docs/remediation-r1/07_R1_W7_Saved_Share_Offline_Forms.md`; record `PROGRESS.md` ("Wave 7 deviations and findings"); evidence `docs/remediation-r1/evidence/w7-*.png`. Commit `d060f1e feat(r1-w7): saved counts and labels, recipient context, offline shell, form validation, branded emails, per-page metadata`.
+
+Saved: the tab badge now counts Want to go only, with "N to go, M been" under the toggle. "Did you make it?" is labelled from the event's own Santa Barbara time and asks once. The empty state links "Browse today" and "Read a guide", and undated saves group under "Places and regulars". Recipient pages: /s, /p and /r share one frame (wordmark, explainer line, "Open SB Daymaker"), and past items are marked everywhere by one `isOver` rule. Offline: it works for the first time. The service worker had never registered, because it waited for a `load` event that had already fired. /saved now serves its cached copy and renders from the device with titles remembered at save time, and every other page falls back to /offline. A dropped connection reads as offline (`ThingsUnreachableError`), never as "No longer listed". Forms: submit validates inline and sets timing. Subscribe validates in the site's styling, keeps the address visible, and no longer reveals who is subscribed: a confirmed address gets a short "already on the list" email and the identical response. Emails: confirm and restore use the edition template with a plain-text alternative, and the cadence lives in `lib/edition/cadence.ts`. Metadata: all nine routes have their own og:title, og:image and description. Every page has header, main, nav and one footer landmark (Explore now uses the shared `PageFooter`). robots.txt keeps search crawlers out of /s/, /p/ and /r/ and lets link-preview bots in. An adversarial review (96 agents) confirmed 39 findings, all fixed and re-verified. This commit also carried early Wave 8 work: `lib/strings.ts`, `CADENCE_LINE`, and the build-failing dash check in `next.config.ts`. Open: Gmail rendering is Jim's to eyeball.
