+## 2026-09-21 · R1 Wave 1: stop the loss
+
+Source: `docs/remediation-r1/01_R1_W1_Stop_the_Loss.md`; baseline `docs/remediation-r1/BASELINE.md`; record `PROGRESS.md`; evidence `docs/remediation-r1/evidence/w1-*.png`; audits `docs/audits/SB_Daymaker_UI_Audit_Log.md` and `docs/audits/2026-09-21-technical-pass.md`. Commit `8a3499b fix(r1-w1): saves resolve by id, pool excludes finished events, share link visible, revalidate after ingest` (it also adds the audits and every R1 spec). Decisions D1, D2 (query half).
+
+The problem: the site was deleting saves. `getPublishedThings()` had no status filter, no date filter and no paging. Once the R1 DDL let anon read archived rows, it served 436 archived rows and lost every evergreen place past PostgREST's 1,000-row ceiling, and /saved deleted anything it could not see. Saves: they now resolve by id through `getThingsByIds()` (published and archived, in chunks of 200) and are never auto-deleted (D1). Unknown ids render "No longer listed" with Remove, and archived ones "Already happened, [date]". `SavesProvider` no longer wipes a list it cannot parse (`sbd.saves.v1.unreadable`). Pool: it filters `status = 'published'` explicitly, drops events finished more than a day ago (`lib/poolFilter.ts`), and pages with `.range()` until the exact count is met, because a larger limit cannot lift the ceiling. `getStopThingMap()` shares the status rule. Backup: the panel shows from the first save. Sharing: a `useShareLink()` sheet shows the URL with Copy whenever native share does not take it, on all five share surfaces. Freshness: `POST /api/revalidate` runs after each successful ingest, and ISR dropped from 600 to 300 s. Baseline: 864 tests in 59 files (the index's 597 was stale); LCP 16.0 s.
+
